      "kind": "phrase",
      "promptEs": "ya no + verbo",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that something used to be true or happen but does not anymore?",
      "answerEn": "Put ya no before the verb to mean “no longer” or “not anymore.”",
      "noteEn": "No supplies the negative meaning, while ya shows that the situation has changed from before. The verb still changes normally for the person and time being discussed.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Ya no vivo en Madrid.",
        "en": "I no longer live in Madrid."
