      "noteEn": "Spanish often uses el, la, los, or las before a body part when the context already makes its owner clear. The verb or another short word can identify the owner. Los is used before a masculine plural body-part word, as in los brazos, where English may naturally say “your arms.”",
      "example": {
        "es": "Levantas los brazos.",
        "en": "You raise your arms."
